import AlgMag.Table.Groups

/-!
# Table 1, rows of rank ≤ 3, checked by the kernel

Each entry is `quantity G = n`, proved by `decide +kernel` (kernel evaluation of the structural
definitions of `AlgMag.Table.Compute`; no `native_decide`).

Root data: Cartan matrix `A i j = ⟨α_i, α_j^∨⟩` (Bourbaki numbering; `B_n`: `α_n` short,
`C_n`: `α_n` long, `G_2`: `α_1` short) and generators of `M` in fundamental-weight coordinates
(`P` = identity, `Q` = rows of `A`). `B_1 = C_1 = A_1`, `D_2 = A_1 × A_1`, `D_3 = A_3`:
`Spin_3 = Sp_2 = SL_2`, `SO_3 = PSp_2 = PGL_2`, `Spin_6 = SL_4`, `SO_6 = SL_4/μ_2`,
`PSO_6 = PGL_4` (same root datum, same row).

Columns: `numRoots` (roots = pure magnets `ℕα`), `numW` (Borel subgroups `⊇ T`), `numBases`
(magnets generated by a basis), `numParabolic` (parabolic subgroups `⊇ T` = pure magnets
containing a basis), `parabolicFormula` (`Σ_J [W : W_J]`), `numFlats` (Levi subgroups `⊇ T`),
`numLeviConj` (`w Φ_J`), `numJoinIrredWeylMagnets`, `numNonRed` (non-redundant Weyl magnets),
`joinIrreduciblesCard`, `nonRedPrimes` (primes of non-redundant Weyl magnets), `pi1Primes`.
-/

namespace AlgMag.Table

set_option maxRecDepth 100000



